{"title":"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 98","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_98&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Convex quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has side-lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab757085426e6962c7d3068e5180cccf07a5cce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=7$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8bf6a33fda7064bc18de335471565522d1147a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=9$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243ec4a88cbb9dc503df328e4485e10e52882633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and there exists a circle, lying inside the quadrilateral and having center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, that is tangent to all four sides of the quadrilateral. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are on the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. It can be proven that point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> always lies on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Supposing further that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/c/bbcfabd65745f2b759dea1840f9a0753b2f992e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, the area of quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> may be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/c/6acf453ce0832b860e02b035914633cdbeaa33b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\sqrt q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/e/deefe999f30fa060a2369f8e0c41a67bbd54d3ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\cdot q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"11\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_.28credit_to_official_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_(credit_to_official_solution)\">Solution (credit to official solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_98&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution (credit to official solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_1.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/76/2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_1.png/300px-2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_1.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"286\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/7/76/2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_1.png 1.5x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Draw lines from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, as seen in the diagram. By SAS Similarity, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b19bd0e9178b3d0c031e3e6bcc92b79dd8862f4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CBA \\sim \\triangle CQM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"147\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633b9fc2818af9930c4212d5f78a115156fb0dde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DBA \\sim \\triangle DNP$\" width=\"146\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/7/147801bbfd796c945d769e12bd4d2870d6175fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12 AB = QM = NP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" />. Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/0/6e02f4e315b77ba3e8ba83242d15d1e426662775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12 CD = QN = MP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"153\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nBecause opposite sides of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873617920310e18cb92b8f61a2c110822412458e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QMPN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> have equal length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/3/873617920310e18cb92b8f61a2c110822412458e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QMPN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelogram\" title=\"Parallelogram\">parallelogram</a>. Thus, the diagonals bisect each other, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82fca277fcf0c962564cf53b271a9bc065da7b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QI = IP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_2.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e9/2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_2.png/300px-2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_2.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"280\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e9/2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_2.png/450px-2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_2.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/e/e9/2008_iTest_Problem_98_Part_2.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2db81fb47bbd461adfa21afffc1424fbc796d740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB \\perp EI$\" width=\"76\" height=\"13\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/b/e8b96ae8fb33723cb8e5b9d517c22346ca52aa92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IF \\perp CD$\" width=\"77\" height=\"12\" />. Also, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/c/76c35555d59e94954491c295eca2adc4c054c1fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IT \\perp BC$\" width=\"75\" height=\"12\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050e8311a80b6c96cc36f186f7ecda7e64c0323e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IS \\perp AD$\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />. By HL Congruency, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d61b463e3fb78303f74db93547cbfdc02748d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ITQ \\cong \\triangle ISP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/a/c0a459ed1924f793d20ecb0880aa6de1dadfc67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS = QT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />. Now we have information we can use to determine side lengths to compute the inradius so we can determine the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/b/dcb5c6989eda3f0303ced16fef69638a22098b83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = AS = AE$\" width=\"111\" height=\"13\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/d/dcd4763d60784a688f7856d777f6b2e17016e8be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB = BT = 7-a$\" width=\"146\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b5296ca337d009e31711630986b3e9b9725f7fd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TC = CF = a+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6eb275e3402622c30ef23ba5a2af87309f1779d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = SD = 13-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"156\" height=\"13\" />. That means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/3/653ff1a97a7ba7cbdea2b11334b0ad6626ad44a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />. Additionally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db1e9253c56212939c6390a3e9bd6bb3eb3614fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP = 6.5$\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/f/04f156a86169952c47fdb604b9f9dbf249fa0630.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BQ = 4.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6024dc38ad18e946a42aee3ad341cf20b9df12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QT = 2.5-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/4/9641f8eed96dab3cfd1f759229029ba29ffaa394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PS = a-6.5$\" width=\"105\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5f5cbb192221607c654db4f627ff472346f1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QT = PS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/3/86351d11d508966a2f5dffaa21364eee6177a268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 4.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nWe know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/c/74ce7d32d65ec3d2112e616cc42eef910fb839b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AIS + \\angle DIS + \\angle BIT + \\angle CIT = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"322\" height=\"14\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad1ef7afb6696633f8cee12139f5b967248061f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\tan(\\angle AIS + \\angle DIS) &amp;= -\\tan(\\angle BIT + \\angle CIT) \\\\ \\frac{\\tan \\angle AIS + \\tan \\angle DIS}{1 - \\tan \\angle AIS \\tan \\angle DIS} &amp;= \\frac{\\tan \\angle BIT + \\tan \\angle CIT}{1 - \\tan \\angle BIT \\tan \\angle CIT} \\end{align*}\" width=\"412\" height=\"64\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of the incircle. That means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a3e020249ab7dce2ac6fbe6af8c3a7390b50eba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\frac{\\frac{4.5}{r} + \\frac{8.5}{r}}{1 - \\frac{4.5 \\cdot 8.5}{r^2}} &amp;= -\\frac{\\frac{2.5}{r} + \\frac{6.5}{r}}{1 - \\frac{2.5 \\cdot 6.5}{r^2}} \\\\ \\frac{13r}{r^2-\\frac{153}{4}} &amp;= \\frac{-9r}{r^2 - \\frac{65}{4}} \\\\ 13r^3 - \\frac{13 \\cdot 65}{4}r &amp;= -9r^3 + \\frac{153 \\cdot 9}{4} \\\\ 22r^2 &amp;= \\frac{13 \\cdot 65 + 153 \\cdot 9}{4} \\\\ r^2 &amp;= \\frac{101}{4} \\\\ r &amp;= \\frac{\\sqrt{101}}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"265\" height=\"273\" />\nTherefore, the area of the quadrilateral is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8ea3fc2115ab0420c15eba21c8a679c14194a3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac12 \\cdot (7 + 9 + 13 + 15) \\cdot \\tfrac{\\sqrt{101}}{2} = 11\\sqrt{101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"292\" height=\"24\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b39bd8f346d0543974d38b39b4d377542b03cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\cdot q = \\boxed{1111}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_98&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest\" title=\"2008 iTest\">2008 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_97\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 97\">Problem 97</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_99\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 99\">Problem 99</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008